phi-adapter-sdk (0.6.0-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Align the log vocabulary with the transport plane and the wire: LogLevel is
    renumbered to 1..5, so enum, wire and phicore::transport::LogLevel are one
    numbering and nothing needs translating at a plane boundary (F-39). Both
    headers static_assert the values, so a renumber fails to compile.
  * Document that adapter log categories live in the shared 0..63 range.
  * ABI: LogLevel values travel by value across the library boundary, so every
    adapter must be rebuilt against this version. An adapter built against the
    0-based header would pass 4 for Error and this library would read it as Warn.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Wed, 19 Aug 2026 23:21:54 +0200

phi-adapter-sdk (0.5.1-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Fix the log level wire encoding: the 0-based C++ enum was cast straight onto
    the 1-based wire (PROTOCOLL.md), so phi-core decoded every adapter log level
    one step too low - sendError() arrived as Warn and Trace (0, out of range)
    arrived as Error. No adapter incident could show up as level=error.
  * sdk_protocol_tests asserts the wire values against the documented table
    instead of against the implementation; the two affected golden fixtures had
    frozen the wrong values.
  * Library-only change: adapters pick it up with the new shared object and do
    not need a rebuild.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Wed, 19 Aug 2026 20:37:07 +0200

phi-adapter-sdk (0.5.0-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Add phi::sdk::kShutdownBudget and SidecarHost::stop(budget): one propagated
    deadline for the whole teardown instead of independent per-step timeouts.
    A sidecar with two instances could previously need ~17s to shut down while
    phi-core kills it 3s after SIGTERM (F-33).
  * Add AdapterInstance::stopRequested() / AdapterFactory::stopRequested(), set
    from the host thread when teardown begins, so blocking adapter code can
    abandon its waits - a thread parked in a socket wait cannot run a queued
    stop().
  * Do not destroy an instance whose execution backend failed to stop: a thread
    may still be running inside it. The runtime is leaked and reported instead
    (was a use-after-free, see F-35).
  * Bounded the Qt backend's post-terminate() grace period to 250ms.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Wed, 19 Aug 2026 18:07:51 +0200

phi-adapter-sdk (0.4.0-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Add AdapterFactory::createFactoryExecutionBackend(): factory-scope hooks can
    now run on their own thread instead of the host poll thread, so a blocking
    device probe no longer stalls IPC for the whole sidecar (F-31). Returns
    nullptr by default, so adapters that do not override it keep the previous
    inline behavior.
  * Add AdapterFactory::onFactoryStopping(), called on the factory execution
    backend before it stops, for destroying thread-affine objects that were
    created lazily inside a factory hook.
  * ABI break: the new virtuals change the AdapterFactory vtable. All adapters
    must be rebuilt against this version.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Wed, 19 Aug 2026 16:43:25 +0200

phi-adapter-sdk (0.3.1-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Remove per-field allocations from the JSON decode path and consume the
    receive buffer with a read cursor instead of memmoving per frame (F-22).
    Internal to the shared library; no API, ABI or wire change.
  * Fix a deadlock: frames are dispatched while the runtime lock is held, so a
    handler that pumps its thread's event loop (nested QEventLoop in blocking
    HTTP/socket helpers) re-entered pollOnce and wedged the sidecar. A
    same-thread re-entrant call is now a no-op (F-30).

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Wed, 19 Aug 2026 14:19:12 +0200

phi-adapter-sdk (0.3.0-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * ABI break (pre-v1, coordinated): AdapterFactory/AdapterInstance state moved
    behind pimpl so future SDK changes no longer break adapter subclasses.
    Adapter sources are unaffected; adapters must be rebuilt.
  * Add runSidecarMain() and SidecarHost::pollDescriptor() so adapters no
    longer hand-roll their main loop (F-27).
  * Use send(MSG_NOSIGNAL): a peer that closed the socket now surfaces as an
    error instead of killing the sidecar with SIGPIPE.
  * Fire onDisconnected/onConnected when a client connection is replaced (F-26).
  * Decode \uXXXX escapes (including surrogate pairs) to UTF-8 (F-21).
  * Reduce MessageType to the implemented frame classes and validate the frame
    class against the command on inbound frames (F-18).
  * Default command timeout 50 ms -> 10 s (F-23).
  * Move the canonical color conversions (HSV/linear/XYZ/xy) into the Qt-free
    phi/adapter/v1/color.h so adapters can translate colors without Qt; the Qt
    wrapper now aliases them and phicore::adapter::Color is one type instead of
    two layout-compatible ones.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Wed, 19 Aug 2026 10:20:56 +0200

phi-adapter-sdk (0.2.0-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Add outbound wakeup (eventfd) so results/events no longer wait for the
    poll timeout; bound frame writes (5s deadline) and the send queue
    (4096 frames with shed policy).
  * Enforce the shared v1 frame payload limit (kMaxPayloadSize, 2 MiB) on
    inbound and outbound frames.
  * Remove the factory-scope AdapterFactory::sendConnectionStateChanged and
    sendAdapterMetaUpdated wrappers; these events are instance-scoped in v1.
  * Add ctest suite: runtime behavior, wire-protocol contract, and
    golden-wire fixtures for all outbound/inbound payloads.
  * Unify the IPC JSON envelope in both directions:
    {"command","cmdId"?,"payload"} with numeric cmdId and all domain
    fields inside payload; consistent externalId/scopeExternalId entity
    fields; stream errors use message; stream data payload key is data.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Tue, 18 Aug 2026 16:00:00 +0200

